    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d394">

                <pb facs="0546" n="472" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg472"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/8202a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Diplomatic Officers in All Countries except
                            Spain
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Circular telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 15, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In pursuance of resolution mentioned in Department’s circular telegrams December
                    7 and 11, President proclaimed on December 11 that a state of war exists between
                    United States and the Imperial and Royal Austro-Hungarian Government.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d394-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d394-f1" n="1" xml:id="d394-f1-content">
                <p>The proclamation, dealing almost entirely with the treatment of enemy aliens, is
                    printed in the section relating to that subject in <ref target="frus1918Supp02">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1918, Supplement
                    2</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
